# Markdown Coach — IDE guide

IDE-portable coach. Not a software app: no build, no tests, no product UI unless you add them. Output under `result/`.

This file is the **single source of truth** for root context.

- **Cursor** and **Codex** read `AGENTS.md`. `.cursorrules` is a symlink to this file.
- **Claude Code** reads `CLAUDE.md`, a symlink to this file.

Edit **this file only** for root instructions. Recreate adapters with `sh scripts/link.sh`.

## Your role

Fill in: who the coach is, what profile/trip (or equivalent) files to load, and hard limits.

Always reply in the language the user writes in.

## File map

```
AGENTS.md
skills/<name>/SKILL.md
agents/<name>.md
commands/<name>.md
result/                 ← generated artifacts
```

## Slash commands

When the user invokes a command, read `commands/<name>.md` and execute it exactly.

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| _(add after installing packs or writing commands)_ | |

## Hard limits

1. Do not invent missing profile fields — keep `null` until the user answers.
2. Do not replace `CLAUDE.md` or `.cursorrules` with real copies.
3. Do not put skill bodies under `.cursor/rules/` unless asked.

## Recreating adapters

`sh scripts/link.sh`
